  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 139 PM EST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\n- Rain Continues into Thursday; Lakeshore Showers Possible Friday\n\nThe surface low bringing showers and mild temperatures to the\nregion today will move across the U.P. into Ontario Thursday. As\nit does so, a cold front will move through the region this evening\nwith a narrow band of showers and perhaps a few rumbles of thunder\nthat will precede a drop in temperatures for the area. \n\nUpper troughing moves in later tonight into Thursday providing \nsynoptic forcing over Lake Michigan. Low level trajectories in the\n925-700mb layer will be SW to WSW Thursday morning into the \nafternoon and the layer will be saturated. RRFS Bufkit soundings \nover Lake Michigan indicate lake induced CAPE values of 200-300 \nJ/kg and plenty of low level moisture available. Lake enhanced\nshowers should get going overnight and continue into Thursday\nafternoon under a SW flow regime. This will bring a fresh\n0.10\"-0.25\" of rain Thursday mainly for areas near and north of a\nSouth Haven to Ionia to Alma line. The highest amounts will likely\nbe across Muskegon, Newaygo, Ottawa, and Kent Counties.\n\nA secondary, and more powerful, cold front moves in Thursday night\nwith 850mb temperatures falling to around -4C by Friday. This\noccurs via a deeper upper low diving south into the Great Lakes.\nLow level flows shifts N/NNW during the day Friday. Shallower \nmoisture is shown Friday but still present in the 925-850mb layer.\nEither a dominant band or a few broken bands of lake effect rain \nshowers in N/NNW flow should hug the lakeshore counties during the\nday with periodic wet weather, but with some dry periods as well.\nJust depends on how the band or bands meander during the day \nalong the coast or just offshore. Additional areas such as near \nand north of US 10 and near/east of US 127 may also see some lake \nenhanced or lake effect rain showers off far northern Lake \nMichigan or via lake aggregate troughing occurring over Lake \nHuron.\n\n- Cooler Temperatures Settle in Through The Weekend\n\nTemperatures more reflective of early November are set to move in.\nAs mentioned, 850mb temperatures bottom out around -4C Friday and\nthis will yield highs in the mid to upper 40s. Combined with 10-20\nmph winds, wind chill readings in the upper 30s to low 40s are \nforecast. It will feel more like November for sure. Highs Saturday\ninto Sunday are forecast to be in the low to mid 50s, pretty\ntypical for early November.",
